  "final_message": "**Analysis**\n\nIn `retry.py:3-9`:\n\n```python\nDEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4\n\ndef call_with_retry(fn, max_attempts=None):\n    attempts = max_attempts if max_attempts is not None else DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS\n    ...\n    for _ in range(attempts):\n```\n\nWhen `max_attempts` is omitted (as in `main7.py`'s `call_with_retry(lambda: 1)`), `attempts` falls back to `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`, and `range(4)` yields exactly 4 iterations \u2014 1 first try plus 3 retries \u2014 before `raise last_exc`.\n\nThe other constants are decoys and never imported by `retry.py`:\n- `decoy_backoff.py`: `RETRY_LIMIT = 5` \u2014 unrelated\n- `decoy_network.py`: `MAX_RETRIES = 3` \u2014 unrelated\n\nANSWER: 4",
